<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Cenprop ups full yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Cenprop ups full yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended December 31.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, div per unit (shr) 26.34  vs  24.98</p>
<p>    Turnover		    54.91  vs  53.06</p>
<p>Total income available</p>
<p>    for distribution	  43.07  vs  40.85</p>
<p>Div payable around February 28</p>
<p>on register February 20</p>
<p>Full name: Centrecity Property Fund (financial - property</p>
<p>trusts)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it would continue its policy of investing in quality properties and maximising its short and medium term return. Assuming the letting of vacant space and the ability of major tenants to meet rental commitments, Cenprop was budgeting for an increase in earnings during the 1997 financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
